Q4. Difference between Traditional Development and TDD.

Interview Ready Answer

Traditional Development

• Code first.
• Testing is done later.
• Bugs are found late.
• More debugging effort.
• Lower confidence while modifying code.
• Refactoring is risky.

------------------------------------------------------------

Test-Driven Development (TDD)

• Test first.
• Testing starts from the beginning.
• Bugs are found early.
• Easier debugging.
• Higher developer confidence.
• Safer refactoring.

======================================================================

Q5. Why do companies prefer TDD?

Interview Ready Answer

Companies use TDD because it produces high-quality software by
detecting defects early and ensuring every feature is automatically
verified before deployment.

Benefits

• Fewer bugs.
• Better software quality.
• Easier maintenance.
• Safer refactoring.
• Faster regression testing.
• Higher developer confidence.

Software/Industry Example

TDD is commonly used in:

• Banking Applications
• FinTech
• Enterprise Spring Boot Applications
• REST APIs
• Microservices
• E-commerce Platforms

